{:event/id "7822b29c-6c84-4a0f-a3d9-ac59e57014d1" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:562817df-4676-4d8f-b502-8f62ce9de2cd" :event/seq 1 :event/causes ["562817df-4676-4d8f-b502-8f62ce9de2cd"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:562817df-4676-4d8f-b502-8f62ce9de2cd" :event/at "2026-08-31T14:09:44Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/schedule-overlap-guard-is-single-flight :finding/shapes #{:gate :state-machine :runtime} :finding/current-name "schedule-id->inflight*" :finding/candidate-name "SingleFlightGate<Key>" :finding/claim "Schedule execution marks one schedule id in flight immediately before awaiting dispatch, refuses a second overlapping tick for that id, and always releases the mark in finally. There is no durable reservation or done state. This is ephemeral keyed exclusion and therefore narrows, rather than generalizes, ReservationGate<Key,Claim>."}}
{:event/id "e7e9761e-0949-41c8-b45d-c3cbfc624a7a" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:562817df-4676-4d8f-b502-8f62ce9de2cd" :event/seq 2 :event/causes ["7822b29c-6c84-4a0f-a3d9-ac59e57014d1"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:562817df-4676-4d8f-b502-8f62ce9de2cd" :event/at "2026-08-31T14:09:44Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/system-instance-is-incarnation-fence :finding/shapes #{:identity :ownership :lifecycle} :finding/current-name "system-instance/current-id + :system_instance_id" :finding/candidate-name "IncarnationFence<OwnerId>" :finding/claim "Knoxx mints one UUID per real backend process, preserves it across shadow-cljs hot reloads, and stamps shared-store documents with that owner id. Equality distinguishes current-instance work from orphaned work only under the documented single-writer law; multi-instance ownership would require a liveness or heartbeat dimension. The reusable shape is an incarnation fence, not a generic process-global cell."}}
{:event/id "b31ee6b8-4cf0-4c4b-a058-84d21aaa6635" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:562817df-4676-4d8f-b502-8f62ce9de2cd" :event/seq 3 :event/causes ["e7e9761e-0949-41c8-b45d-c3cbfc624a7a"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:562817df-4676-4d8f-b502-8f62ce9de2cd" :event/at "2026-08-31T14:09:44Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/defonce-runtime-state-is-reload-stable-not-durable :finding/shapes #{:cell :lifecycle :infra} :finding/current-name "runtime.state registers + lifecycle/http-state*" :finding/candidate-name "ReloadStableCell<T>" :finding/claim "Several defonce atoms intentionally survive shadow-cljs route reloads while the HTTP app is closed and recreated; wider process services remain alive. Their lifetime is module-reload-stable but process-local and non-durable. This refines the seed Cell<T> vocabulary with an explicit lifetime law instead of treating defonce as persistence."}}
{:event/id "c0481c19-a69d-4983-b013-6c9d6f5c03d6" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:562817df-4676-4d8f-b502-8f62ce9de2cd" :event/seq 4 :event/causes ["b31ee6b8-4cf0-4c4b-a058-84d21aaa6635"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:562817df-4676-4d8f-b502-8f62ce9de2cd" :event/at "2026-08-31T14:09:44Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/ingestion-admission-is-bounded-work-queue :finding/shapes #{:queue :backpressure :infra} :finding/current-name "ThreadPoolExecutor + ArrayBlockingQueue" :finding/candidate-name "BoundedWorkQueue<Work>" :finding/claim "The ingestion executor has an explicit admission law: four core workers, up to eight workers, a queue capacity of 1000, and rejected submission reported as false when capacity is exhausted. CPU EMA pacing and OpenPlanner failure penalties live beside it but obey different algorithms, so bounded admission should not be collapsed into a generic backpressure service."}}
{:event/id "a6f34d21-47c5-4b8d-9e12-6d53c298f741" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:562817df-4676-4d8f-b502-8f62ce9de2cd" :event/seq 5 :event/causes ["c0481c19-a69d-4983-b013-6c9d6f5c03d6"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:562817df-4676-4d8f-b502-8f62ce9de2cd" :event/at "2026-09-01T17:30:00Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/ingestion-feedback-policies-are-distinct :finding/shapes #{:feedback :pacing :backoff :infra} :finding/current-name "cpu EMA pacing + OpenPlanner failure penalties" :finding/candidate-name "FeedbackPolicy<Signal,Delay>" :finding/claim "Ingestion feedback control is distinct from bounded queue admission and contains two adjacent algorithms that must remain distinguishable: CPU pacing derives delay from an exponential moving average of load, while OpenPlanner failure handling applies recovery penalties after failed downstream work. They may both delay ingestion, but they consume different signals and encode different recovery laws, so neither is evidence for BoundedWorkQueue<Work> and they should not be collapsed into one generic backpressure mechanism."}}
